\section{Full contact network versus incomplete abstraction}
\label{sec:information_view}

Let $\calF_t$ represent the full information generated by the microscopic contact network and node states up to time $t$. A two-scale model operates with a smaller information set $\calI_t\subseteq\calF_t$. This smaller information set may contain the community partition, local microstates inside simulated communities, aggregate community counts, and macro weights $W_{ij}$, but not all cross-community endpoint states and edges.

