\section{Theoretical results: what information is valuable?}
\label{sec:value_information}

This section gives the core theoretical results. They are stated for the full CTMC and the two-scale abstraction above. The guiding variable is the full-information cross-community intensity
\begin{equation}
  Y_{ij}(t)=a^\star_{ij}(X(t)).
\end{equation}
A reduced model that sees only $\calI_t\subseteq\calF_t$ cannot generally use $Y_{ij}(t)$ itself. It must predict it from the retained information.

