\section{Chains of cliques and accumulation of prediction loss}
\label{sec:chain_cliques}

A single clique--bridge--leaf motif isolates one interface. A chain of cliques repeats the same information bottleneck along a path of communities. Let communities $0,1,\ldots,L-1$ each contain a clique of size $n$. For each consecutive pair $(\ell,\ell+1)$, a bridge set in community $\ell$ connects to one or more entry nodes in community $\ell+1$. The epidemic starts in community $0$ and must cross interfaces sequentially.

